  "spec": "specs.md §23.2",
  "description": "A record of the log, as a process writes it on standard error with log_format = \"json\": one line of OpenTelemetry's log data model, with the field names of its specification, in this order: Timestamp, the Unix nanoseconds as a string of digits, left out with no time; SeverityText, slog's name of the level; SeverityNumber, the level plus 9, from 1 to 24; Body; Attributes, left out when there is none; Resource; InstrumentationScope, left out with no scope. A string attribute that is not valid UTF-8 goes under its key and _b64, as base64 of its bytes; the body and the strings of a list take one U+FFFD for each run of bytes that are not.",
